Look, there's a hole in it.

261
00:15:25,583 --> 00:15:27,986
I'm serious, Al.
I need your help.

262
00:15:28,019 --> 00:15:31,156
I'm not cool like you.

263
00:15:31,189 --> 00:15:34,159
If the older kids find me,
they're gonna beat me up.

264
00:15:34,192 --> 00:15:36,261
Yeah, man, you're right.

265
00:15:36,294 --> 00:15:37,996
What should I do?
I'm freaking out.

266
00:15:38,029 --> 00:15:40,731
Uh, how cool is the other kid?

267
00:15:40,765 --> 00:15:43,401
He's pretty cool.
He always has dope clothes.

268
00:15:43,434 --> 00:15:45,536
His dad is, like, 30.

269
00:15:45,570 --> 00:15:46,804
Man, don't be acting nervous.

270
00:15:46,837 --> 00:15:49,074
I mean, people try
to come at you, just deny it.

271
00:15:49,107 --> 00:15:50,141
Confidence is the key.

272
00:15:50,175 --> 00:15:52,877
All right?

273
00:15:52,910 --> 00:15:55,580
Hold it down, cuzzo.
Heading to lunch.

274
00:15:55,613 --> 00:15:57,615
Okay.

275
00:16:03,321 --> 00:16:05,023
MRS. WILLIAMS: Make sure
you finish your packets

276
00:16:05,056 --> 00:16:06,691
and bring them in tomorrow.

277
00:16:06,724 --> 00:16:08,726
I'm going to place a bin
on my desk.

278
00:16:08,759 --> 00:16:10,295
I want you to put them in there.

279
00:16:10,328 --> 00:16:12,230
And cite your work, folks.

280
00:16:12,263 --> 00:16:15,266
The Internet is not a source...

281
00:16:15,300 --> 00:16:16,901
-All right,

282
00:16:16,934 --> 00:16:18,769
names at the top
of your packets.

283
00:16:18,803 --> 00:16:22,373
That's an easy 50 points.
Good job.

284
00:16:37,722 --> 00:16:39,557
Wait, Earn!

285
00:16:39,590 --> 00:16:41,859
Johnny? Guess who I found.
Check it out.

286
00:16:41,892 --> 00:16:43,061
Oh, this shit crazy.

287
00:16:43,094 --> 00:16:44,929
Let me see the tag.

288
00:16:48,666 --> 00:16:50,435
This one's fake!

289
00:16:50,468 --> 00:16:51,736
It says "made in Bangladesh."

290
00:16:51,769 --> 00:16:52,803
It should be China.

291
00:16:52,837 --> 00:16:53,971
I knew he was wrong as hell.

292
00:16:55,673 --> 00:16:57,875
Hey, yo, his shirt fake, y'all!
Yo!

293
00:16:57,908 --> 00:16:59,777
Hold up, hold up,
hold up, hold up, hold on.

294
00:16:59,810 --> 00:17:01,112
Let me see.

295
00:17:08,153 --> 00:17:09,487
Let me see.

296
00:17:09,520 --> 00:17:11,756
Man, this one the real shirt.

297
00:17:11,789 --> 00:17:15,326
It's supposed to say "made in
Bangladesh" on this one.

298
00:17:15,360 --> 00:17:18,863
Of course this fool gonna say
"made in China." He is Chinese.

299
00:17:18,896 --> 00:17:20,898
-Come on, man.

300
00:17:20,931 --> 00:17:23,134
That one the fake one.
Trust me, I know.

301
00:17:24,802 --> 00:17:27,605
Man, my shirt ain't fake.
It ain't.

302
00:17:27,638 --> 00:17:29,140
CHRIS:
Yo, this nigga homeless!

303
00:17:29,174 --> 00:17:31,309
Devin rockin' fake FUBU now.

304
00:17:31,342 --> 00:17:33,344
JOHNNY:
I'm not Chinese. I'm Filipino.

305
00:17:50,061 --> 00:17:51,929
Wait. Here you go, Earn.

306
00:17:51,962 --> 00:17:54,199
You know, that's my number,
if you want to call me.

307
00:17:54,232 --> 00:17:55,366
But only between 6:00 and 9:00.

308
00:17:55,400 --> 00:17:56,601
O-Okay, cool.

309
00:17:56,634 --> 00:17:59,537
-See you tomorrow, Earn.
-See ya.

310
00:18:02,673 --> 00:18:05,976
Yo. I can't believe this fool
tried to lie on you.

311
00:18:06,010 --> 00:18:07,612
Yeah, it's crazy.

312
00:18:07,645 --> 00:18:09,080
Yeah, 12th-graders
just found out.

313
00:18:09,114 --> 00:18:10,715
They're going in on this man.

314
00:18:22,026 --> 00:18:24,229
-Damn.

315
00:18:24,262 --> 00:18:26,231
Hey, FEBE, man.

316
00:18:28,333 --> 00:18:30,668
OLDER KID: You finna cry
or something

317
00:18:45,950 --> 00:18:48,586
("Passing Me By" by The Pharcyde
playing)

318
00:18:48,619 --> 00:18:51,322
GIRL : Band practice
will be moving to Room G today

319
00:18:51,356 --> 00:18:53,090
due to a leak in the ceiling.

320
00:18:53,124 --> 00:18:55,092
That is Room G.

321
00:18:55,126 --> 00:18:57,695
Just a reminder,
the book fair is this Tuesday.

322
00:18:57,728 --> 00:18:59,497
If you have any books
you want to donate,

323
00:18:59,530 --> 00:19:01,966
you can trade them
with Mr. Johnson...

324
00:19:04,402 --> 00:19:05,370
Spirit Week is next week.

325
00:19:05,403 --> 00:19:07,738
We will be doing Pajama Day,

326
00:19:07,772 --> 00:19:10,575
Sports, Crazy Hair,
and '80s Day...

327
00:19:33,831 --> 00:19:36,100
Everyone, please settle down.

328
00:19:45,976 --> 00:19:49,914
I came to let you all know
something very serious.

329
00:19:49,947 --> 00:19:53,884
Your classmate, Devin Myers,
committed suicide last night.

330
00:19:56,687 --> 00:19:58,556
We're not sure why,

331
00:19:58,589 --> 00:20:01,091
but we've heard
a couple of things.

332
00:20:01,125 --> 00:20:03,928
It seems Devin's parents
had just gotten divorced,

333
00:20:03,961 --> 00:20:06,931
and he was dealing with it
pretty hard.

334
00:20:06,964 --> 00:20:09,434
Now, if anybody needs to talk
about what happened,

335
00:20:09,467 --> 00:20:12,102
please visit Mrs. Lindell
in the counselor's office.

336
00:20:12,136 --> 00:20:16,006
Mrs. Banks or any other teacher
will write you a pass.

337
00:20:16,040 --> 00:20:18,809
Thank you, Mrs. Banks.

338
00:20:25,216 --> 00:20:27,585
MRS. BANKS:
I think it's good to remember

339
00:20:27,618 --> 00:20:30,321
that we all have

340
00:20:30,355 --> 00:20:33,023
personal things going on
in our life

341
00:20:33,057 --> 00:20:34,825
that other people may not
know about.

342
00:20:36,694 --> 00:20:38,463
So...

343
00:20:38,496 --> 00:20:40,631
-Hi, Mrs. Banks.
-Oh, hello, Denisha.

344
00:20:43,601 --> 00:20:46,971
MRS. BANKS:
But... let's try to be

345
00:20:47,004 --> 00:20:49,173
more understanding
of one another.

346
00:20:51,208 --> 00:20:55,145
Okay, um, turn to page 45

347
00:20:55,179 --> 00:20:56,481
in your books.

348
00:20:56,514 --> 00:20:59,984
And, uh, who wants to read?

349
00:21:00,017 --> 00:21:02,520
-I'll do it, Mrs. Banks.
-Okay.

350
00:21:06,924 --> 00:21:09,193
Whenever you're ready.

351
00:21:18,035 --> 00:21:20,204
Hey.

352
00:21:20,237 --> 00:21:22,607
You look tired.

353
00:21:22,640 --> 00:21:25,175
No, I'm okay.
Just a long day.

354
00:21:25,209 --> 00:21:28,379
Maybe you need to start going to
bed sooner and stop staying up.

355
00:21:28,413 --> 00:21:31,382
Hey, Earn.
-Hey, Auntie.

356
00:21:31,416 --> 00:21:34,018
GLORIA:
I got a call from the school.

357
00:21:34,051 --> 00:21:36,754
One of your classmates died.

358
00:21:36,787 --> 00:21:38,689
-Yeah, Devin.
-Hmm.

359
00:21:38,723 --> 00:21:40,291
-Kind of.

360
00:21:40,325 --> 00:21:43,561
That's so sad.
She seemed to think

361
00:21:43,594 --> 00:21:45,430
maybe some of the older boys
were messing with him.

362
00:21:45,463 --> 00:21:50,167
You better say something
if somebody tries harassing you.

363
00:21:50,200 --> 00:21:52,169
People will bully you
your whole life if you let 'em.

364
00:21:52,202 --> 00:21:53,771
-Yeah, they will.
-You got to stand up
for yourself.

365
00:21:53,804 --> 00:21:54,772
Mm-hmm, and you and your cousin

366
00:21:54,805 --> 00:21:57,575
got to look out for each other.

367
00:21:57,608 --> 00:21:59,577
You guys look out
for each other, now.

368
00:21:59,610 --> 00:22:02,780
Boy, get your feet
out that chair.

369
00:22:02,813 --> 00:22:04,214
GLORIA: You start
piano lessons tomorrow.

370
00:22:04,248 --> 00:22:06,817
-Yeah, I'm ready.

371
00:22:06,851 --> 00:22:08,786
I'm gonna lay out
a suit for you,

372
00:22:08,819 --> 00:22:11,121
so you'll need to add
a black belt.

373
00:22:11,155 --> 00:22:12,757
A suit?
Why I got to wear that?

374
00:22:12,790 --> 00:22:14,559
Because I said so.

375
00:22:14,592 --> 00:22:15,893
You want to make
a good impression.

376
00:22:15,926 --> 00:22:17,462
Our mother always said,

377
00:22:17,495 --> 00:22:19,730
"You got one chance to make
a first impression."

378
00:22:19,764 --> 00:22:21,231
LORRAINE:
Mm-hmm. True indeed.

379
00:22:21,265 --> 00:22:23,033
But it's gonna be all hot...

380
00:22:23,067 --> 00:22:24,301
GLORIA:
I don't care.

381
00:22:24,335 --> 00:22:26,971
You are a black man in America,

382
00:22:27,004 --> 00:22:29,807
and when you meet people,
you need to look good.

383
00:22:29,840 --> 00:22:31,909
Your clothes are important.

384
00:22:31,942 --> 00:22:35,846
That's true, Earn.
You need to wear the suit.

385
00:22:39,450 --> 00:22:41,151
GLORIA:
Oh, and I got you another one

386
00:22:41,185 --> 00:22:42,787
of those FUBU shirts.

387
00:22:42,820 --> 00:22:44,422
It was on sale.

388
00:22:44,455 --> 00:22:47,324
Don't say I never did
anything for you.

389
00:22:47,358 --> 00:22:48,793
Thanks.

